WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Oil sands operations contribute significant carbon emissions in Canada. So the six largest companies have teamed up to make strides on the path to NetZero. Investing in technology and innovation. Already cut emissions in average 22% per barrel. Working with governments to create and protect jobs. Developing one of the world's largest carbon capture and storage facilities. Our NetZero plan is in motion and we're making progress on multiple pathways. See our plan in action at pathwaysalliance.ca
加拿大油砂开采产生了巨量的碳排放。因此，六家最大的公司携手合作，在迈向“净零”的道路上大步迈进。他们投资于技术和创新。每桶碳排放量平均已减少22%。他们与政府合作，创造并保护就业岗位。并正在建设世界上最大的碳捕集与储存设施之一。我们的“净零”计划正在推进中，我们正通过多种途径取得进展。请访问 pathwaysalliance.ca 了解我们的行动计划。

2
00:00:30.000 --> 00:01:19.000
Music On the 1st of December 1948, the body of a man was located along the seawall of Summerton Beach, just near Red Alive, in South Australia. At first the case received very little media attention and the police thought it was a pretty straightforward matter. The natural death on the beach, no big deal, just had to ID the body and it would all be over. But as the weeks and months went on it soon became apparent that this case was anything but straightforward and the further you dug into it, the deeper it went. To this day we don't know who he is, we don't know where he came from and we don't know how he died.
音乐。1948年12月1日，在南澳大利亚州红活区（Red Alive）附近的萨默顿海滩（Summerton Beach）海堤旁，发现了一具男子的尸体。起初，这起案件几乎没有引起媒体的关注，警方也认为这是一件非常简单直接的事情。海滩上的自然死亡，没什么大不了的，只要确认死者身份，一切就都结束了。但随着几周和几个月的过去，人们很快发现，这起案件绝不简单，你挖得越深，牵扯就越深。直到今天，我们仍然不知道他是谁，不知道他来自哪里，也不知道他是怎么死的。

3
00:01:19.000 --> 00:02:05.000
Welcome to the mysterious case of the Summerton Man. Music On Wednesday the 1st of December 1948, the body of an unknown man was found on Summerton Beach in Adelaide, South Australia. The unknown man would come to be known as the Summerton Man. He remains one of Australia's most baffling mysteries. He was found lying on the sand with his head propped up resting against the seawall. It's a pretty uncomfortable awkward position. To this day his identity and cause of death remain a mystery.
欢迎收听萨默顿男尸谜案。音乐。1948年12月1日星期三，在南澳大利亚州阿德莱德的萨默顿海滩上发现了一具身份不明男子的尸体。这个神秘男子后来被称为“萨默顿人”。他至今仍然是澳大利亚最令人迷惑的谜团之一。人们发现他躺在沙滩上，头部斜靠着海堤。这是一个相当不舒服、别扭的姿势。直到今天，他的身份和死因依然是个谜。

4
00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:44.000
Like all mysterious and unsolved cases there are many theories and a lot of wild speculation. And in this case there's a lot of information to fuel these theories and wild speculation. The Summerton Man was found with no identification. In fact even the labels from the clothes he was wearing had been removed. To this day he remains unidentified. He was found with a crumbled up piece of paper in his pocket containing two words. Taman should, which is Persian meaning finished or ended. These words were later linked to a poultry book which contained what many believed to be a secret code.
像所有神秘且未破的案件一样，这里有许多理论和大量的疯狂猜测。而在本案中，有大量的信息来助长这些理论和疯狂猜测。人们发现萨默顿人身上没有任何身份证明。事实上，连他所穿衣服上的标签都被剪掉了。直到今天，他的身份依然是个谜。人们发现他的口袋里有一张揉成一团的纸，上面写着两个字：Taman should，在波斯语中意思是“完结”或“结束”。这些字后来与一本诗集联系在一起，其中包含许多人认为的密码。

5
00:02:44.000 --> 00:03:30.000
Along with the code there was two phone numbers, that of a local bank and one of a local Adelaide woman who lived only about 400 metres away from where the Summerton Man was found. The Adelaide woman said she had no idea who the Summerton Man was but many believed she was lying. Like most unsolved cases there are plenty more questions than answers. But let's start with what we do know and to do that we need to go back to Adelaide, 1948. The Summerton Man arrived at Adelaide train station on the day before his body was found, Tuesday 30th November 1948. Once arriving at the station he checked his suitcase into the plug room. The suitcase was tagged and the receipt was given to the Summerton Man.
除了密码之外，还有两个电话号码，一个是当地银行的，另一个是当地一位阿德莱德女性的，她住的地方离发现萨默顿人的地方只有大约400米远。这位阿德莱德女性说她根本不知道萨默顿人是谁，但许多人认为她在撒谎。像大多数未破案件一样，疑问远比答案多。但让我们从已知的事实开始，为此我们需要回到1948年的阿德莱德。萨默顿人在被发现死去的头一天，即1948年11月30日星期日（注：原文Tuesday为周二，按上下文修正或直译），到达了阿德莱德火车站。一到车站，他就把手提箱寄存在了行李寄存处。手提箱贴上了标签，收据交给了萨默顿人。

6
00:03:30.000 --> 00:04:14.000
From a time stamp found on the suitcase tag is determined that he checked it in somewhere around 11am. The only train arriving to Adelaide around that time that was from a big city was a train from Melbourne. All the other trains arriving into Adelaide were from smaller country locations. So it's commonly thought he most likely came from Melbourne as a non-identified mystery man walking around with a suitcase probably would have stood out in a smaller country location. The locals out there don't miss too much. After checking in the suitcase the Summerton Man bought a train ticket to go from Adelaide station to Henley Beach. It was a second class one-way ticket although nothing could really be taken away from that as all tickets on that line were second class. There was no first class.
根据行李标签上的时间戳，可以确定他大约在上午11点左右办理了寄存。当时到达阿德莱德且来自大城市的唯一一列火车是一列来自墨尔本的火车。所有其他到达阿德莱德的火车都来自较小的乡村地区。因此人们普遍认为他最能来自墨尔本，因为一个身份不明的神秘男子带着手提箱在较小的乡村地区四处走动可能会非常显眼。那里的当地人对周遭的事情可是了如指掌。寄存完手提箱后，萨默顿人买了一张从阿德莱德火车站到亨利海滩（Henley Beach）的火车票。这是一张二等单程票，不过这其实说明不了什么，因为该线路上的所有票都是二等票。根本没有一等票。

7
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:55.000
Within the time frame of him checking his suitcase in there were two departures to Henley Beach. One at 10.50am and the other at 11.51am. But the Summerton Man didn't get on either train as the ticket was found unused in his pocket. Instead of boarding a train he walked across the road and bought a bus ticket to Glenelg. The bus departed at 11.15am and dropped him off about a 20 minute walk away from where he was found dead on Summerton Beach. Now Henley Beach for where he had the unused train ticket was 7km away from where he was found. So that's a pretty long walk. The thought is he probably bought that train ticket as Henley Beach was the closest train station to where he had to go
在他寄存手提箱的时间范围内，有两趟开往亨利海滩的列车。一趟在上午10点50分，另一趟在上午11点51分。但萨默顿人并没有坐这两趟车中的任何一趟，因为那张票在他的口袋里被发现时完好未动。他没有上火车，而是穿过马路，买了一张去格莱内尔格（Glenelg）的汽车票。这辆巴士于上午11点15分出发，把他放在距离他在萨默顿海滩被发现死亡的地方大约步行20分钟的地方。而他原本有未使用火车票的亨利海滩，距离他被发现的地方有7公里远。所以那是一段相当长的步行路程。大家的想法是，他可能买了那张火车票，因为亨利海滩是他要去的地方最近的火车站

8
00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:38.000
not realising that there was a bus that got him a lot closer. So after talking to someone or even seeing a sign he bought the bus ticket and didn't worry about the train ticket. He jumped on board the bus would have been an old double decker back then and made the journey to Glenelg. Getting there around lunchtime. What he did after getting off the bus is anyone's guess because there's no sight of the Summerton Man again until about 7.15pm that evening. At 7.15pm a local businessman John Lyons and his wife were going for a walk along Summerton Beach. The sun was starting to set about this time. Here they saw the Summerton Man lying on the beach head propped up against the sea wall body laying out on the sand.
却没有意识到有一辆公交车能把他带得离目的地近得多。所以在跟人聊过天或者甚至看到了一个标志后，他买了公交车票，而不再管那张火车票了。他跳上了一辆公交车——在当时那应该是一辆老式的双层巴士——前往格莱内尔格。并在午餐时间左右到达那里。他下车后做了什么，谁也说不准，因为直到那天晚上大约7点15分，萨默顿人才再次被人看到。晚上7点15分，当地的一位商人生产约翰·莱昂斯（John Lyons）和他的妻子正在萨默顿海滩散步。这时太阳开始落山了。在这里，他们看到萨默顿人躺在沙滩上，头部斜靠着海堤，身体舒展地躺在沙滩上。

9
00:05:38.000 --> 00:06:11.000
Just like when he was found dead. Although he wasn't dead because he raised his right arm up and then flopped it down. They didn't think too much of it they just put it down to another drunk who had won too many and was now sleeping it off and they continued on their walk. Now should be noted this is not a quiet isolated spot. There were plenty of people who used the beach and walked along the Esplanade. It was a popular location. He was laying right next to a set of stairs which led up to the Esplanade and these stairs were used regularly. About 8pm that night a young couple were going for a walk along the Esplanade.
就像他被发现死去时一样。不过他当时还没死，因为他把右臂举了起来，然后又啪地放下了。他们当时没太在意，只认为这是又一个喝多了、宿醉未醒的酒鬼，于是继续他们的散步。现在应该指出的是，这不是一个安静偏僻的地方。有很多人使用这个海滩并沿着海滨大道（Esplanade）散步。这是一个很受欢迎的地方。他就躺在一组通往海滨大道的台阶旁，而这些台阶经常被人使用。那天晚上大约8点，一对年轻夫妇正沿着海滨大道散步。

10
00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:50.000
It was just on dusk. They sat down on a bench right next to the staircase where the Summerton Man was laying down below on the sand. Here they saw an unknown man in a hat standing at the top of the steps. He appeared to be looking down at the Summerton Man. This man was never identified and was never seen or heard from again. No one knows if he's related to the case or not. The young couple looked down and they could see the legs of the Summerton Man but their view of the top half of his body was blocked by the staircase. They didn't see him move but they did report that by the time they'd left the bench they thought his position had changed.
当时正值黄昏。他们坐在紧挨着台阶的长椅上，而萨默顿人就躺在下方沙滩上的台阶旁。在这里，他们看到一个戴帽子的陌生男子站在台阶顶端。他似乎正低头看着萨默顿人。这个男人从未被识别身份，也再也没有被看到或听到过。没人知道他是否与此案有关。这对年轻夫妇往下看，可以看到萨默顿人的腿，但他们对上半身的视线被台阶挡住了。他们没有看到他移动，但他们确实报告说，当他们离开长椅时，他们觉得他的位置已经变了。

11
00:06:50.000 --> 00:07:32.000
They commented that they thought it was strange that he wasn't moving because the mosquitoes were bad. But they didn't go in for a closer look and as they thought his position had changed they thought everything was okay. They got up and left and they didn't see anyone else before leaving. About 6am the next morning, Wednesday the 1st of December, two jockies were each riding a horse down on the beach. They rode past the Summerton Man but like John Lyons and his wife their initial thoughts were that it was just a drunk sleeping off a bender. However when they rode back up the beach they realised that he hadn't moved. He was in the exact same spot his head propped up against the seawall. It's a pretty awkward, unnatural looking position.
他们评论说，他们觉得奇怪的是他怎么一动不动，因为那里的蚊子很厉害。但他们没有走过去仔细查看，而且由于他们觉得他的位置变了，他们认为一切都好。他们起身离开了，在离开之前没有看到其他人。第二天早上6点左右，即12月1日星期三，两个骑马的骑师正骑着马在海滩上。他们骑马从萨默顿人身旁经过，但就像约翰·莱昂斯和他的妻子一样，他们最初的想法这只是一个宿醉的酒鬼在醒酒。然而，当他们骑马返回海滩时，他们意识到他根本没有动。他还在原来的地方，头部斜靠着海堤。这是一个相当别扭、看起来很不自然的姿势。

12
00:07:32.000 --> 00:08:05.000
They went in to see if he was alright but he wasn't. The Summerton Man was dead. Now at this time John Lyons was actually back at the beach. He was going for a morning swim with a friend. The jockies and the bit of commotion caught his eye and he immediately recognised the Summerton Man as the same person he and his wife had seen the night before. He rushed over and called the police. Police officer John Moss was the first to arrive at the scene. He got there at about 6.45.
他们走过去看他是否还好，但并不是。萨默顿人已经死了。此时，约翰·莱昂斯其实已经回到了海滩。他正和朋友进行晨泳。骑师和一些骚动引起了他的注意，他立即认出萨默顿人就是他和妻子前天晚上看到的那个人。他冲过去并报了警。警官约翰·莫斯（John Moss）是第一个到达现场的人。他大约在6点45分到达。

13
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:55.000
He examined the scene and he found a half smoke cigarette that had fallen between the Summerton Man's cheek and his collar but there were no burn or blister marks on his face or clothing. The sands surrounding him wasn't disturbed, his clothing wasn't ruffled or dishevelled, there was no debris or personal items scattered around the beach. Basically he determined there were no signs of violence at all. A check of the Summerton Man's pockets found the unused train ticket, the bus ticket, two combs, one aluminium and one plastic. The aluminium came as thought to be from America as they were pretty rare in Australia at the time or they weren't actually available at all I don't think. A packet of juicy fruit chewing gum and a packet of Army Club cigarettes. But the cigarettes inside the packet of Army Clubs weren't Army Club, they were a different brand, Considus. There was also a box of Bryant and May's matches.
他检查了现场，发现在萨默顿人的脸颊和衣领之间掉落了一根抽了一半的烟，但他的脸部或衣服上没有烧焦或起泡的痕迹。他周围的沙子没有被扰动，他的衣服没有凌乱或散乱，海滩上也没有散落碎片或私人物品。基本上，他断定根本没有暴力的迹象。检查萨默顿人的口袋，发现了一张未使用的火车票、公交车票、两把梳子（一把铝制，一把塑料制）。那把铝制的梳子被认为是来自美洲，因为当时在澳大利亚它们非常罕见，或者我认为根本买不到。一包多汁水果口香糖和一包军团俱乐部（Army Club）香烟。但是军团俱乐部烟盒里的香烟不是军团俱乐部，而是另一个品牌——康西达斯（Considus）。还有一个布莱恩特和梅（Bryant and May）的火柴盒。

14
00:08:55.000 --> 00:09:43.000
It was common at the time for people to buy an expensive brand of cigarettes, keep that box and then fill it up with cheaper cigarettes. It was just an image thing. But the funny thing about the Summerton Man is that the Considus cigarettes were the more expensive brand. Far more expensive than the Army Club box that he had. So this could have been a sign of someone who was trying to keep a low profile. An ambulance was called and they took the body to Royal Adelaide Hospital where a doctor came out and pronounced the Summerton Man dead. The time of death was estimated to be no earlier than 2am. But that is now considered to be a very rough estimate as the methods used to estimate the time of death back then not quite as good as what they do today.
当时人们很流行购买昂贵的香烟品牌，保留那个盒子，然后装满便宜的香烟。这只是一种营造形象的做法。但关于萨默顿人有趣的是，康西达斯香烟反而是更贵的品牌。比他拥有的军团俱乐部烟盒贵得多。所以这可能是某人试图保持低调的迹象。有人叫了救护车，他们把尸体送到皇家阿德莱德医院，在那里一位医生出来宣布萨默顿人死亡。死亡时间估计不早于凌晨2点。但现在这被认为是一个非常粗略的估计，因为当时用来估计死亡的方法不如今天那么好。

15
00:09:43.000 --> 00:10:45.000
The post-mortem was performed the next day. Now what immediately stuck out about the Summerton Man was that he was a physical specimen in incredible shape, well-built, classic V-shaped body of an athlete. Someone physically strong yet he had very smooth hands with no calluses indicating that he didn't work in any job involving manual labour or heavy use of the hands. His hands were also described as being enormous. His fingernails and toenails were well cared for. And along with his impressive upper body physique he also had unusually well-developed calf muscles with a bulge near the knee. The coroner thought this was a sign that he may have been a professional dancer or a ballet performer or something similar. He was described or estimated to be about 45 years old, about 80 kilos. He was a Caucasian male. He was missing about 16 teeth overall but that wasn't at all uncommon at the time. In fact there's probably more common than not.
尸检于第二天进行。关于萨默顿人，立刻让人眼前一亮的是，他是一个身体健壮、体格惊人的男子，身材魁梧，具有运动员经典的V型身材。一个身体强壮的人，然而他却有着非常光滑的手，没有老茧，这表明他没有从事任何涉及体力劳动或大量使用双手的职业。他的手也被描述为大得惊人。他的手指甲和脚趾甲都修剪得很整洁。除了令人印象深刻的上半身体格外，他的小腿肌肉也异常发达，膝盖附近有隆起。法医认为这表明他可能是一名职业舞蹈演员、芭蕾舞演员或类似的人。据描述或估计，他大约45岁，重约80公斤。他是一个高加索白人男性。他总共缺了大约16颗牙齿，但这在当时一点也不罕见。事实上，这可能比不缺牙更常见。

16
00:10:45.000 --> 00:11:38.000
Another unusual thing about the Summerton Man is that his spleen was three times the size of a normal spleen. Now this indicates a pre-existing illness that would not have happened quickly overnight at the time of his death. So I thought that he'd been carrying it for a while. It's evidence that he might have already been in a weakened state when he died. In large spleens can be a result of many illnesses including viral and bacterial infections, inflammatory diseases, even some cancers can cause that. He also had yellow stained hands indicating that he was a heavy smoker. His actual cause of death that was not immediately obvious but there were no signs of foul play so it was thought to be a natural death. His heart stopping although his heart was healthy so they couldn't put their finger on it straight away.
萨默顿人的另一个不同寻常之处在于，他的脾脏是正常脾脏的三倍大。这表明他患有某种既往疾病，这种疾病在他死时绝不是一朝一夕突然发生的。所以我认为他已经带病一段时间了。这证明他在死时可能已经处于虚弱状态。巨大的脾脏可能是许多疾病的结果，包括病毒和细菌感染、炎症性疾病，甚至某些癌症也会导致这种情况。他的双手呈黄色，表明他是个老烟民。他的真正死因并没有立即显现出来，但没有他杀迹象，所以被认为是一起自然死亡。他的心脏停止了跳动，尽管他的心脏很健康，所以他们无法马上找出原因。

17
00:11:38.000 --> 00:12:36.000
The police certainly weren't treating it as a suspicious death in the early stages. They were convinced it wouldn't be too long before a relative or friend came forward and identified the body and the case would be finalised. A lot of people did come forward to try and identify the body as a missing relative or friend but no positive idea was made. After a few days it started to become a bit of a concern and on the 10th of December a decision was made between banning the body to preserve it in the hopes that in the coming days or weeks somebody would eventually show up and identify the body and the case could be finalised. But no one ever did. It didn't take long before the investigators, the medical people actually started to deviate off the natural death path and onto an unnatural death path. As I already said he had a healthy heart, there was no sign of heart disease or anything like that so there's nothing to suggest that his heart would just stop due to a heart attack or something.
在早期阶段，警方肯定没有把它当作可疑死亡来处理。他们确信，不久就会有亲戚或朋友站出来认领并确认尸体，然后案件就会结案。许多人确实站出来试图认领尸体，说他是失踪的亲戚或朋友，但没有做出确切的身份确认。几天后，这开始成为一个令人担忧的问题，12月10日，人们做出了一个决定：对尸体进行防腐处理以将其保存下来，希望在接下来的几天或几周内，最终会有人出现并确认尸体，从而结案。但没有人出现。没过多久，调查人员和医学人员就开始偏离自然死亡的道路，走上了非自然死亡的道路。正如我刚才所说，他有一颗健康的心脏，没有心脏病或类似迹象，所以没有任何迹象表明他的心脏会因为心脏病发作或其他原因而骤停。

18
00:12:36.000 --> 00:13:33.000
